  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: Nested Loop
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: 'Just like <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>if</color></font>
    statements, loops can also be placed inside other loops! This is called a <color=yellow>nested
    loop</color>.


    When a loop is nested, the inner loop must finish all of
    its repetitions before the outer loop can move on to its next step. This makes
    nested loops perfect for working with 2D coordinates, like scanning rows and
    columns on a map!


    The goal for this level is to traverse every single grid
    on the map in one program run. You can achieve this by using an outer loop for
    the rows and an inner loop for the columns.


    Hint: <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF">(i % <color=#B5CEA8>2</color> == <color=#B5CEA8>0</color>)</font> can be
    used to check whether <font="JetBrainsMono SDF">i</font> is an even number.

    This
    works because even numbers have no remainder when divided by <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#B5CEA8>2</color></font>.'
  isImageBig: 0
